# Sevalla static-site redirects.
# https://docs.sevalla.com/static-sites/redirects  (verified 2026-08-20)
#
# Sevalla reads this file from the root of the published directory. Rules are
# applied top to bottom and the FIRST match wins, so the domain-level rule has
# to come before the path rules or www would be served rather than redirected.
#
# Supported here: 301, 302, 200 (rewrite), and a "!" suffix to force a rule even
# when a real file exists at that path.

# --- www -> apex ----------------------------------------------------------
# laytr.app is the one canonical Laytr domain. Serving both hosts would split
# search ranking and widen cookie scope, so www is a permanent redirect and
# never an origin of its own.
#
# Sevalla's _redirects matches a full URL including the hostname, which is why
# this belongs here rather than in host configuration. Both laytr.app AND
# www.laytr.app must still be added as domains in the Sevalla dashboard, each
# with its own DNS record and its own certificate, or this rule never runs
# because nothing terminates TLS for www (website/README.md §10).
https://www.laytr.app/*   https://laytr.app/:splat   301!

# --- canonical paths ------------------------------------------------------
# The .html forms are reachable because the host serves them; send them to the
# clean URL so one page never has two live addresses.
/index.html      /            301
/privacy.html    /privacy     301
/terms.html      /terms       301
/support.html    /support     301
/welcome.html    /welcome     301

# --- aliases people and documents actually type ---------------------------
/privacy-policy  /privacy     301
/policy          /privacy     301
/tos             /terms       301
/eula            /terms       301
/help            /support     301
/contact         /support     301
